 ## Overview
-Sparse Volume Textures (SVT) is a volume rendering technique in Unreal Engine 5 that renders large, sparse volumetric datasets (up to ~6 gigavoxels) by sampling data stored in sparse tiles within a large volume texture [S1, S2, unofficial][S3]. It solves the problem of integrating sparse, potentially animated 3D data into the rendering pipeline using standard material nodes, circumventing the DirectX 11 API limit of contiguous memory allocation for large textures [S2, unofficial][S3]. Unlike debug viewers or fog-specific renderers, it supports full lighting, emission, and color, making it suitable for scientific data visualization [S1, unofficial]. It builds on [Sparse Volume Texture Setup](7432-sparse-volume-texture-setup.md) by defining the material and actor workflow required to visualize the data [S3].
