 **Formulas and Parameters:**
-*   **UV Coordinates:** $UV \in [0, 1]^3$. The UV space spans the union of bounding boxes of individual frames [S3].
-*   **Lighting Step Size:** $Step = Factor \times Resolution$. Increasing `Lighting Step Factor` takes longer steps, sacrificing quality for performance [S4].
-*   **Shadow Step Size:** $Step = Factor \times Resolution$. Increasing `Shadow Step Factor` takes longer steps, sacrificing quality for performance [S4].
-*   **Shadow Bias:** Adjusts the initial voxel bias applied when calculating shadows. Increasing it reduces self-shadowing but may introduce light leaking [S4].
-*   **Lighting Cache Resolution:** $Resolution_{cache} = Resolution_{SVT} / LightingDownsampleFactor$. The cache is dense and does not allocate a volume resolution greater than $1024 \times 1024 \times 512$ voxels [S4].
-*   **Streaming Mip Bias:** Controls the texture level. Lower values equate to higher density and quality; higher values have less density and quality [S4].
